## `ItemLike`

`ItemLike` is an interface implemented by `Item`s and [`Block`s][block] in vanilla. It defines the method `#asItem`, which returns an item representation of whatever the object actually is: `Item`s just return themselves, while `Block`s return their associated `BlockItem` if available, and `Blocks.AIR` otherwise. `ItemLike`s are used in various contexts where the "origin" of the item isn't important, for example in many [data

potion set on it. This is an informal term, the vanilla `PotionItem` class has nothing to do with this (it refers to the "normal" potion item). Minecraft currently has four potion items: potions, splash potions, lingering potions, and tipped arrows; however more may be added by mods.

